A tier namespace becomes a path segment under `--out`, so one that is not a plain root name is
rejected before anything is written.

-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  specs:
    tiers:
      core:
        path: ~/core-specs
        namespace: ../escape
-- fixtures/home/core-specs/value/0001-small-steps.md --
---
type: value
title: Small steps
summary: Ship in small, reviewable steps.
kind: value
---

# Small steps
-- cmd --
booping specs site
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
-- stderr --
error: core.specs.tiers.core.namespace `../escape` must match [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]* to name a site root
